\newlabel{fig:06-book}{{6.1}{92}{A limit order book. Sellers' asks sit above the midpoint and buyers' bids below it. A buyer who wants to trade at once pays the best ask, \$50.02; a seller receives the best bid, \$49.98. The gap of \$0.04, 8 basis points of the \$50.00 midpoint, is the bid--ask spread}{figure.caption.35}{}}
